    {
      "id": "news-christianacare-epic",
      "slug": "christianacare-epic-go-live",
      "kind": "news",
      "title": "ChristianaCare sets Oct. 3, 2026 Epic go-live",
      "dek": "The Wilmington system is in the final stage. Patients keep appointments unless contacted.",
      "body": "ChristianaCare is cutting its clinical record, caregiver workflows, and patient tools over to Epic on Oct. 3, 2026. A July 2026 update put the Wilmington system in the final stage, less than three months out. COO Ric Cuming said caregivers must finish on-demand and live role-based training, and pass readiness checks, before they use the new system. Patients keep appointments unless contacted. After go-live they move to ChristianaCare MyChart for results, visit summaries, scheduling, messaging, eCheck-in, refills, and bill pay. Care Everywhere will share records with participating Epic organizations when a patient is treated off-campus. ChristianaCare said that once it is live, all Delaware health systems, and many more in Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Maryland, will also be on Epic.",
      "status": "published",
      "featured": false,
