    {
      "id": "news-jefferson-fy2026-loss",
      "slug": "jefferson-fy2026-operating-loss",
      "kind": "news",
      "title": "Jefferson posts $181.5 million operating loss for FY2026",
      "dek": "Bondholder results published by The Inquirer on Aug. 14, 2026 included $112 million in layoff and related costs.",
      "body": "Thomas Jefferson University and Jefferson Health posted a $181.5 million operating loss for the year ended June 30, 2026, in results reported to bondholders and published by The Philadelphia Inquirer on Aug. 14, 2026. The results included $112 million in layoff and related costs. Jefferson closed on Lehigh Valley Health Network on Aug. 1, 2024. Chief financial officer Michael Harrington told The Inquirer that commercial-insurer actions in Pennsylvania threaten those gains. Jefferson sued Independence Blue Cross last month over contract reinterpretations and sued Aetna in April over Medicare Advantage stay payments. Independence said it acts for its customers. Aetna said its policies comply with federal law. The $181.5 million loss does not move until a court or a new contract does.",
      "status": "published",
      "featured": false,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-14T16:00:00.000Z",
